WEBVTT

00:16.558 --> 00:22.188
DOROHEDORO

01:35.804 --> 01:37.931
THE BEGINNING

01:38.014 --> 01:43.978
GOLDEN BEETLES ARE RICH

01:45.605 --> 01:46.940
Okay, this is the place.

01:47.899 --> 01:49.275
Woah, it's huge!

01:49.776 --> 01:52.737
So... this is the Landlord's mansion, eh?

01:53.655 --> 01:54.906
Alright, here's the plan.

01:55.406 --> 01:58.785
We have to make it look like she died
naturally in her own home.

01:58.868 --> 02:02.622
Because if En finds out she died at
our place... then things are gonna get

02:02.705 --> 02:03.748
real messy indeed.

02:05.792 --> 02:07.669
Hey, Saji. What are you doing?

02:07.752 --> 02:10.421
Our embroidery side hustle. The
deadline's today.

02:14.968 --> 02:17.178
She actually had security cameras
installed!

02:17.262 --> 02:18.221
Ugh rich people.

02:18.721 --> 02:19.764
They're gross!

02:21.057 --> 02:23.059
Hey guys... Look, over there.

02:26.479 --> 02:27.981
That's the main security unit.

02:28.690 --> 02:30.316
If we can somehow disable it,

02:30.400 --> 02:32.777
then the security cameras should stop
working.

02:32.861 --> 02:33.903
Ton.

02:41.578 --> 02:43.329
Distance to target looks like...

02:43.413 --> 02:46.249
it'll be around Thirty-Five meters. Okay...

02:48.126 --> 02:49.002
Got it.

03:04.309 --> 03:08.229
Amazing! Ha! What a awesome shot
you crazy pig!

03:10.106 --> 03:10.940
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

03:11.024 --> 03:12.108
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

03:12.775 --> 03:14.569
To unlock, please insert smoke.

03:14.652 --> 03:16.237
To unlock, please insert smoke.

03:16.738 --> 03:18.573
The front door has a smoke lock...

03:18.656 --> 03:21.951
The door won't open unless we have some
of the Landlord's smoke.

03:22.035 --> 03:23.828
What do you think we should do?

03:23.912 --> 03:26.247
We can't waste any more time hanging
around outside...

03:26.331 --> 03:29.500
Okay! Looks like this is where I come in!

03:50.230 --> 03:51.981
How'd ya like my super strength!?

03:52.899 --> 03:53.733
- Wow!
- Wow!

03:54.234 --> 03:56.527
Whatever, let's hurry up and get inside.

03:57.362 --> 03:59.822
It's so dark out here I can't see my
embroidery.

03:59.906 --> 04:02.075
Seriously? Why the hell did you
come here?

04:02.575 --> 04:03.826
So... heavy...

04:05.245 --> 04:07.622
She must weigh about Four-Hundred kilos!

04:07.705 --> 04:08.581
So much space.

04:09.082 --> 04:10.166
This is just the hall?

04:10.250 --> 04:12.794
Well, let's steal something when we
leave here.

04:13.628 --> 04:15.004
Toilet paper would be good.

04:17.257 --> 04:18.424
Seeing something like this...

04:18.508 --> 04:20.426
I can't help but feel a little guilty.

04:21.052 --> 04:22.011
Let's just hurry up.

04:22.095 --> 04:24.597
This death needs to look as natural as
possible.

04:27.267 --> 04:30.395
When you think about most of the
accidents that happen at home.

04:30.478 --> 04:33.147
Accidentally drowning in the bath tub
is one of them.

04:36.276 --> 04:37.777
The temperature's just right!

04:38.319 --> 04:40.488
Hang on... Almost there...

04:41.072 --> 04:41.906
Damnit.

04:43.491 --> 04:44.325
I did it!

04:46.703 --> 04:47.537
Heave!

04:54.794 --> 04:55.712
Very natural.

05:01.050 --> 05:05.013
If we wrap the rope around her like this,
we can make it look like she chose to

05:05.096 --> 05:05.930
end her life.

05:06.764 --> 05:08.099
Dokuga... You write it?

05:08.766 --> 05:09.600
Yeah.

05:12.103 --> 05:13.104
It's natural, right?

05:14.856 --> 05:16.649
Hey! Coming down!

05:17.150 --> 05:18.234
Yeah, go ahead.

05:18.735 --> 05:19.694
- Ready, and...
- Ready, and...

05:19.777 --> 05:21.070
By the way, Dokuga.

05:21.154 --> 05:23.489
Who was the person you saw killing Risu?

05:24.240 --> 05:25.825
Was it someone we already know?

05:27.618 --> 05:29.120
That's it, come on.

05:30.330 --> 05:33.207
Also, you not being able to kill Risu...

05:33.833 --> 05:34.834
Is that really true?

05:36.085 --> 05:37.337
Yeah. It's all true.

05:37.837 --> 05:40.673
Are you kidding? There's no way you
wouldn't be able to.

05:47.764 --> 05:48.639
That's the thing...

05:50.683 --> 05:51.517
The issue

05:52.018 --> 05:53.561
Is to do with Risu's magic.

05:54.520 --> 05:56.397
Risu's... Magic?

06:00.068 --> 06:01.652
- Dokuga!!!
- Dokuga!!!

06:06.282 --> 06:07.158
Dokuga!

06:17.085 --> 06:19.921
Ah! What the hell is that!?!

06:23.466 --> 06:24.467
Dokuga!!

06:29.847 --> 06:33.726
Oh! I know what this thing is! It's a
diet insect!

06:33.810 --> 06:37.647
If you keep one of those in your stomach,
then it absorbs whatever you eat!

06:37.730 --> 06:39.357
So it came out after she died?

06:40.108 --> 06:43.027
Ah well.
This all looks pretty natural to me.

06:43.111 --> 06:44.070
Which part?

06:44.862 --> 06:47.198
- Dokuga!
- Let's just take what we can and leave!

06:47.281 --> 06:48.116
I got you, come on!

06:48.199 --> 06:50.451
Oh! Look I've finally finished my
embroidery!

06:51.536 --> 06:54.831
I just hope it will end up becoming some
lovely lady's handkerchief.

06:54.914 --> 06:56.249
Come on let's go!

06:57.667 --> 07:00.628
Wow! What wonderful embroidery!

07:00.711 --> 07:03.881
It's really nice that girls get to enjoy
such lovely underwear!

07:07.635 --> 07:10.847
Near the entrance of hell... there
lies a small store that remains

07:10.930 --> 07:12.056
nameless.

07:13.015 --> 07:14.851
CUTE BUTCHER

07:20.731 --> 07:22.859
Woah, no way. What kind of store is this?

07:23.359 --> 07:24.944
One that sells meat.

07:25.528 --> 07:27.530
But I don't see a shopkeeper anywhere.

07:28.656 --> 07:32.076
That's because you're still a devil
trainee... you can't see him yet.

07:32.160 --> 07:34.328
Look... you can see his shadow, right?

07:35.163 --> 07:39.876
He's neither a devil or a sorcerer...
he's neither good or evil.

07:43.713 --> 07:46.507
- I'll take some meat.
- Na na na na...

07:49.510 --> 07:51.053
So what is this meat then?

07:52.638 --> 07:56.350
It's the meat of a certain creature.
Once you eat it, your body will start

07:56.434 --> 07:57.727
turning into a devil.

07:59.187 --> 08:00.313
Na na na...

08:06.068 --> 08:07.695
Thanks, I'm counting on you.

08:10.198 --> 08:14.744
Asu... you kept a secret from us. From your
own comrades.

08:16.120 --> 08:18.247
That's something I cannot forgive.

08:19.415 --> 08:21.042
I just made a call to Store.

08:21.667 --> 08:24.170
You know what that means, don't you? Asu...

08:42.605 --> 08:44.649
You are no longer fit to be a devil.

08:44.732 --> 08:45.775
Asu.

09:10.341 --> 09:11.217
Store, you're up.

09:11.884 --> 09:12.718
He's all yours.

09:49.839 --> 09:52.258
Here... Store... That's for you.

09:53.467 --> 09:54.844
Na na na na

09:56.095 --> 09:58.806
Asu. You are such a fool.

10:00.516 --> 10:02.268
No. You're no longer 'Asu'.

10:02.768 --> 10:05.313
Kawajiri the Sorcerer, wasn't it?

10:07.481 --> 10:08.733
Farewell, Kawajiri.

10:09.233 --> 10:12.278
You can go back to living as a
Sorcerer now.

10:17.074 --> 10:20.953
My power.
I can feel it fading away from me...

10:21.704 --> 10:22.830
Nikai...do...

10:28.419 --> 10:29.754
EAST ZAGAN TORQUE

10:29.837 --> 10:31.047
Come and get 'em!

10:31.130 --> 10:34.258
Anybody want some freshly baked bread?
They're filled with lots of cheese, lots

10:34.342 --> 10:36.761
of stew and a whole lotta cream.

10:36.844 --> 10:37.970
I'll take three, please!

10:38.054 --> 10:38.888
Coming up!

10:43.934 --> 10:46.937
Wow you really are eating that with your
mask on, aren't you?

10:47.021 --> 10:50.274
So I'm the one paying for these? Okay
that's fine, they're on me!

10:53.986 --> 10:55.237
Mmmm... yum!

10:55.946 --> 10:57.239
Aah, cheesy!

11:05.915 --> 11:10.753
Come and get 'em. Freshly baked bread
with stew, cheese and cream...

11:13.589 --> 11:16.258
Na... na na... na na na... na na...

11:20.388 --> 11:25.309
The evening before I turned Asu
back from a devil to just a sorcerer.

11:27.311 --> 11:30.147
I feel so much more at ease with my own
mask on.

11:30.731 --> 11:33.025
Oh this is bad, the evening just flew by!

11:33.109 --> 11:34.568
I really should go to bed.

11:35.820 --> 11:39.323
But first things first. I need to
find a good hiding place for my mask

11:39.407 --> 11:41.117
so I can keep it safe and sound.

11:41.200 --> 11:44.745
Nope there's no way I'm hiding it
down here it'll certainly be found.

11:44.829 --> 11:46.997
Oh maybe somewhere in here?

11:50.793 --> 11:52.586
What's this? A notebook?

11:53.087 --> 11:54.672
Could it belong to Nikaido?

11:55.548 --> 11:57.007
I see it has a smoke lock?

11:58.676 --> 11:59.802
No problem!

12:00.553 --> 12:02.972
A lock like this is nothing against my
magic!

12:08.269 --> 12:10.730
MY HEART'S DIARY

12:11.272 --> 12:13.023
"My heart's diary..."

12:14.150 --> 12:16.569
This girl has no taste whatsoever!

12:17.278 --> 12:18.279
Alright, let's see...

12:18.779 --> 12:22.158
"I feel as though the power of the
devil's contract inside of me is

12:22.241 --> 12:23.075
crushing me"

12:23.159 --> 12:25.536
If this carries on, I may disappear
completely.

12:26.871 --> 12:30.374
But before that happens. I've decided
I should write about my magic in

12:30.458 --> 12:31.292
this diary.

12:32.877 --> 12:35.963
So that even when I'm completely
controlled by the contract...

12:36.046 --> 12:38.257
I will never use my magic.

12:38.340 --> 12:40.050
DOOR TO THE PAST

12:43.137 --> 12:45.681
I grew up in a tiny village deep in the
mountains.

12:46.390 --> 12:49.393
Although my parents passed away when I
was only a baby.

12:50.519 --> 12:52.354
I was always a happy child.

12:53.189 --> 12:56.525
I had a kind auntie and uncle...
and Kawajiri... who always looked out

12:56.609 --> 12:59.153
for me. Treated me like he was my big
brother.

12:59.945 --> 13:01.572
Every day there was fun.

13:02.782 --> 13:05.701
That was until my best friend, Yakumo, disappeared.

13:07.286 --> 13:08.704
I can't go on! Too tired!

13:09.288 --> 13:11.040
I'll read the rest of it tomorrow.

13:14.585 --> 13:18.547
Alright, everyone. I want to hear your
opinion on a new product I'm planning on

13:18.631 --> 13:19.882
selling under my brand.

13:19.965 --> 13:22.343
It's called... "The En-shaped Mushroom
Doll."

13:22.968 --> 13:25.471
It's an edible mushroom pet made for
my fans.

13:25.971 --> 13:27.306
It's awesome!

13:28.724 --> 13:31.393
They react to things like humidity
and airflow.

13:31.477 --> 13:32.561
So cute!

13:33.562 --> 13:34.480
I must have one!

13:36.690 --> 13:40.152
Although they're prone to becoming
parasites, attaching themselves to

13:40.236 --> 13:41.946
living beings. I'll work on that.

13:42.029 --> 13:43.322
What do you think?

13:43.405 --> 13:45.407
I'd like to hear your opinion, Nikaido.

13:45.491 --> 13:46.784
Well, let's see...

13:46.867 --> 13:49.495
Ooh I know! It'd be great if they were
bigger!

13:49.578 --> 13:51.747
Y'know, if they were the same size
as you!

13:51.831 --> 13:53.207
Good opinion, Nikaido!

13:53.707 --> 13:54.750
Approved!

13:54.834 --> 13:55.709
Oh, yay!

13:55.793 --> 13:59.380
Stop it! Please! Someone take this thing
off of me!

14:00.506 --> 14:01.799
By the way, Nikaido...

14:02.299 --> 14:04.510
Do you still not feel like using your
magic?

14:05.302 --> 14:06.804
I don't want to talk about it!

14:06.887 --> 14:07.805
Wait!

14:07.888 --> 14:11.308
Nikaido!
I'm sorry! I didn't mean to force you!

14:11.851 --> 14:12.685
Nikaido...

14:15.020 --> 14:16.981
Oh wow. That caught me off guard.

14:17.481 --> 14:21.068
Although pretending to be upset and
running away from him won't work much

14:21.151 --> 14:22.111
longer.

14:22.194 --> 14:23.529
I worked up quite a sweat.

14:24.029 --> 14:26.991
Maybe I should take a bath and continue
reading that diary.

14:30.160 --> 14:31.912
Aaaaah, right...

14:32.663 --> 14:35.416
It wasn't until I was around two or
three years old...

14:35.499 --> 14:37.960
That I was first able to properly use
magic.

14:40.671 --> 14:42.590
Wow, Nikaido, that's great!

14:47.094 --> 14:49.179
- What is this?
- A candy?

14:49.680 --> 14:52.766
Well, whatever it is, I'm sure
you'll figure it out eventually

14:52.850 --> 14:54.435
Once you make more smoke!

14:54.518 --> 14:56.186
Nikaido will practice!

14:56.270 --> 14:57.229
Hey!!

14:58.022 --> 15:00.190
Kawajiri! Nikaido!

15:00.274 --> 15:01.275
Yakumo!

15:02.443 --> 15:04.904
Yakumo's magic gave her the ability to
fly!

15:07.156 --> 15:10.534
When she was a baby, she was found
floating down the river by sheer

15:10.618 --> 15:11.452
coincidence.

15:12.202 --> 15:15.372
Because of that, she always used
to say that she had great luck

15:15.456 --> 15:16.457
wherever she went.

15:17.875 --> 15:21.086
She was always so cheerful... and wasn't
afraid of anything.

15:25.007 --> 15:26.634
Oh no, it's another dead child.

15:26.717 --> 15:27.551
I'm scared!

15:27.635 --> 15:29.887
That means there must be some hunters
nearby.

15:30.471 --> 15:32.431
We should leave here right now.

15:32.514 --> 15:36.518
Hunters... they were people who
would kidnap Sorcerer children.

15:37.603 --> 15:41.649
Many children died because of fighting
between different groups of hunters.

15:42.691 --> 15:43.609
Young man...

15:44.693 --> 15:46.362
Leave those kids here and go.

15:46.445 --> 15:48.238
You see, one of mine just died.

15:48.322 --> 15:49.323
It's a hunter!

15:49.823 --> 15:51.909
Asshole! I'll punch you!--

15:58.749 --> 15:59.875
They vanished!

16:01.001 --> 16:05.464
Kawajiri was a Sorcerer... His magic
allowed him to travel anywhere freely.

16:06.256 --> 16:09.635
He also had a kind of clairvoyance.
Which meant he could choose his

16:09.718 --> 16:10.552
destination.

16:11.136 --> 16:12.471
Hello, Auntie! We're back.

16:13.597 --> 16:17.267
Kawajiri... You really should stop
relying on magic all the time and try to

16:17.351 --> 16:19.311
walk a little once in a while.

16:19.395 --> 16:20.354
He's right.

16:20.437 --> 16:22.731
We only just managed to escape from a
hunter.

16:23.774 --> 16:25.150
We're eating gyozas today!

16:25.651 --> 16:28.112
Gyozas were always Auntie's specialty.

16:29.321 --> 16:30.906
I wonder what Gyozas are?

16:30.990 --> 16:34.535
I guess I'm really not too familiar with
the food of the commoners.

16:35.160 --> 16:35.995
Oh well.

16:36.078 --> 16:38.539
It was around the time that I was four
years old...

16:42.334 --> 16:43.794
What are you both doing?

16:43.877 --> 16:45.254
Welcome home, Kawajiri!

16:45.921 --> 16:48.215
I'm training Nikaido so she knows how to
fight!

16:48.298 --> 16:50.551
It's good. Now I know how to break
boards.

16:50.634 --> 16:52.845
Yeah, but aren't you bleeding, though?

16:52.928 --> 16:54.346
This is too much, Yakumo.

16:54.847 --> 16:57.766
But this is the only way her fists
will ever get stronger.

16:58.892 --> 17:00.936
- What is that?
- Huh?

17:01.020 --> 17:02.771
Oh! This thing?

17:04.440 --> 17:07.818
I got it the other day from a devil who
gave me his business card.

17:07.901 --> 17:09.737
He made it especially for me.

17:10.529 --> 17:11.363
So cool!

17:12.614 --> 17:15.034
I've been given an invitation to become a
devil.

17:25.627 --> 17:27.838
Make sure you do your best, Kawajiri.

17:28.338 --> 17:31.258
That armor's very impressive. Will you
be okay?

17:31.341 --> 17:35.179
Yeah... apparently living every day life in
this thing is the first phase of

17:35.262 --> 17:36.388
training.

17:37.431 --> 17:39.183
Well, I'm off to work.

17:40.684 --> 17:42.519
What's the point if he doesn't walk?

17:43.520 --> 17:47.066
That day... I was in the house on
my own for the first time.

17:47.816 --> 17:52.321
As soon as I finished wrapping the gyoza...
I realized I had nothing else to do.

17:55.324 --> 17:58.827
A thought then dawned... It had been
a while since I used my magic... so I

17:58.911 --> 18:00.829
tried letting out some smoke.

18:04.374 --> 18:07.711
Maybe it was because I was a bit
older, my power had increased...

18:07.795 --> 18:10.506
But the cube was almost the same size
as me.

18:12.091 --> 18:14.510
It also now had buttons and levers on it.

18:15.094 --> 18:18.305
I tried pressing all the buttons
and pulling all the levers... but

18:18.388 --> 18:19.556
nothing seemed to work.

18:20.682 --> 18:25.437
I decided that in order to master my
magic... I needed to start practicing.

18:29.608 --> 18:33.946
What I didn't know... was that would be the
beginning of a terrifying event...

18:34.446 --> 18:35.280
Nikaido!

18:35.364 --> 18:37.950
- En!
- It's me! Open up!

18:38.534 --> 18:41.203
I'm here to apologize! I also brought you
presents!

18:41.870 --> 18:44.373
Just when things were getting
interesting.

18:44.456 --> 18:46.375
I really do need to dry my hair first...

18:47.251 --> 18:48.085
What?

18:50.671 --> 18:51.505
The hell?

18:51.588 --> 18:52.756
THE PLACE OF CONFORT BERITH

18:52.840 --> 18:56.051
Seriously?! Now you're saying you
don't know the location of the

18:56.135 --> 18:57.302
Cross-Eyes hideout?!

18:57.970 --> 18:58.804
Well. No...

18:59.471 --> 19:01.390
I just wanted to travel with you both!

19:01.890 --> 19:02.724
Sorry...

19:02.808 --> 19:05.686
But... I'm sure we'll find it if
we look for it!

19:06.186 --> 19:07.437
How can we do that?

19:08.188 --> 19:10.149
We have absolutely no information.

19:10.232 --> 19:12.109
Also it'll be getting dark soon.

19:12.192 --> 19:15.028
Right, well let's find somewhere to
rest for the night!

19:15.112 --> 19:17.447
Then we can start our search tomorrow
morning!

19:19.491 --> 19:20.450
What do you think?

19:20.534 --> 19:21.493
Caiman?

19:22.286 --> 19:23.120
Huh?

19:24.037 --> 19:25.038
Uh yeah...

19:27.541 --> 19:28.375
Caiman...

19:30.002 --> 19:30.836
But...

19:30.919 --> 19:33.922
Will there even be a place to stay
in such a small village?

19:34.548 --> 19:35.799
Yeah, you're right...

19:35.883 --> 19:39.386
BERITH HOT SPRINGS

19:39.469 --> 19:40.888
Oh, how about this place?

19:40.971 --> 19:42.764
Welcome one and all!

19:43.265 --> 19:46.268
It looks like three guests have arrived!

19:48.770 --> 19:51.523
A married couple... and their child.

19:52.900 --> 19:54.818
MAGMA BATH

19:54.902 --> 19:56.195
Nikaido, please open the door!

19:56.278 --> 19:58.363
- Oh no...
- Nikaido!

19:58.447 --> 20:00.407
What should I do? I'm back to me again!

20:03.035 --> 20:03.869
Ouch!

20:04.870 --> 20:07.247
- Huh?
- What happened, Nikaido?! Are you okay?

20:07.748 --> 20:12.085
Isn't this... the contract from En that was
inside Nikaido's body?

20:16.006 --> 20:16.840
Nikaido!

20:18.842 --> 20:21.595
Nikaido... I'm sorry about earlier... I--

20:21.678 --> 20:24.640
I for-give-you-hon-ey-bu--

20:25.140 --> 20:28.644
Chota! You stupid bird! What the
hell do you think you're doing here?

20:28.727 --> 20:30.354
I can explain everything!

20:31.730 --> 20:32.564
What?!

20:33.273 --> 20:35.692
Nikaido actually ran away with
that lizard man?!

20:36.443 --> 20:38.737
So... that means the Nikaido that was here...

20:38.820 --> 20:40.614
Heh, surprise! That was me--

20:40.697 --> 20:41.949
Turn to mushroom!

20:42.950 --> 20:45.285
I'm sorry! I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

20:52.084 --> 20:53.710
It's so busy all of a sudden...

20:54.836 --> 20:55.671
Ah well...

20:55.754 --> 20:58.423
I wonder where Ebisu's gone off to?
She skipped work.

20:58.966 --> 21:01.677
Even though we got our salary today
from the Big Boss.

21:01.760 --> 21:03.011
Not that it's much.

21:05.639 --> 21:09.268
I guess she isn't an official member of
the family anyway, so it doesn't

21:09.351 --> 21:12.062
really matter.
She just stuck around for no reason.

21:12.145 --> 21:14.982
In fact, now might be a good time to
kick her out!

21:16.108 --> 21:16.942
Ebisu?

21:19.695 --> 21:21.071
I wonder where she's going?

21:21.613 --> 21:22.948
And with all that luggage...

21:24.616 --> 21:26.660
No way... Is she leaving?

21:30.080 --> 21:32.749
Fine then, go if you want... I don't
give a damn.

21:35.002 --> 21:35.836
Ebisu!

21:43.343 --> 21:45.012
Hey... where you going?

21:45.887 --> 21:46.763
I'm going home.

21:47.514 --> 21:49.308
Wait, what? So does that mean...

21:49.808 --> 21:51.560
did you get your memories back?

21:53.145 --> 21:54.896
Bye bye... Fujita.

23:30.784 --> 23:31.910
THE END

23:31.993 --> 23:33.745
What we learned in Episode 16.

23:33.829 --> 23:36.540
Store sells a certain creature's meat.

23:36.623 --> 23:38.083
Natsuki is the one who pays.

23:38.166 --> 23:39.668
En found out many things.

23:39.751 --> 23:41.878
What we're going to learn in Episode 17:

23:41.962 --> 23:43.713
It's still... lost in chaos.

23:43.797 --> 23:46.425
This is... Dorohedoro!
